'''Sandro Tonali''' ({{IPA|it|ˈsandro toˈnaːli}}; born 8 May 2000) is an Italian professional [[Association football|footballer]] who plays as a [[midfielder]] for {{English football updater|TottenhH}} club [[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur]] and the [[Italy national football team|Italy national team]].

He began his professional career at [[Brescia Calcio|Brescia]], winning [[Serie B]] in [[2018–19 Serie B|2018–19]]. A year later he moved to [[AC Milan|Milan]], initially on loan. He played 130 total games for Milan, and won [[Serie A]] in [[2021–22 Serie A|2021–22]]. In 2023, he signed for Newcastle for a reported fee of €70&nbsp;million, becoming the most expensive Italian footballer of all time.

==Club career==
===Brescia===
Tonali made his professional debut for [[Brescia Calcio]] on 26 August 2017, aged 17, coming on as a substitute in the [[Serie B]] away match lost 2–1 against [[US Avellino 1912|Avellino]].<ref>{{cite web|publisher=Soccerway|url=https://int.soccerway.com/matches/2017/08/26/italy/serie-b/us-avellino/brescia-calcio/2560032/|title=Game Report by Soccerway|date=26 August 2017|access-date=21 February 2018|archive-date=15 June 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180615095220/https://int.soccerway.com/matches/2017/08/26/italy/serie-b/us-avellino/brescia-calcio/2560032/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 28 April 2018 he scored his first professional career goal, in a 4–2 defeat against [[US Salernitana 1919|Salernitana]] in Serie B.<ref name="primo gol">{{cite web|author1=Angelo Taglieri|date=28 April 2018|title=Tonali, primo gol in carriera: Juve e Inter lo hanno già chiesto, il Milan...|url=https://www.calciomercato.com/news/tonali-primo-gol-in-carriera-juve-e-inter-lo-hanno-gia-chiesto-i-69224|access-date=14 October 2018|publisher=calciomercato.com|language=Italian|archive-date=12 May 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190512041052/https://www.calciomercato.com/news/tonali-primo-gol-in-carriera-juve-e-inter-lo-hanno-gia-chiesto-i-69224|url-status=live}}</ref> He obtained 19 league appearances in total during his first season as a professional player, scoring two goals and providing two assists during the [[2017–18 Serie B]] season.<ref name="next Pirlo">{{cite web|author1=Nikita Fesyukov|date=14 October 2018|title=Introducing Tonali, 'the next Pirlo' wanted by Sarri and Allegri|url=https://www.calciomercato.com/en/news/introducing-tonali-the-next-pirlo-wanted-by-sarri-and-allegri-12923|access-date=14 October 2018|publisher=calciomercato.com|archive-date=12 May 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190512041051/https://www.calciomercato.com/en/news/introducing-tonali-the-next-pirlo-wanted-by-sarri-and-allegri-12923|url-status=dead}}</ref>

The following season, Tonali won the [[2018–19 Serie B|Serie B title]] with Brescia, and achieved promotion to Serie A, featuring as a starter for the club throughout the entire 2018–19 season.<ref name="Brescia back in business">{{cite web |url=https://www.football-italia.net/141215/brescia-back-business |title=Brescia back in business |publisher=Football Italia |last1=Rahaman |first1=Vijay |date=26 July 2019 |access-date=25 September 2019 |archive-date=28 October 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201028162320/https://www.football-italia.net/141215/brescia-back-business |url-status=live }}</ref>

He made his Serie A debut on 25 August 2019, aged 19, in a 1–0 away win against [[Cagliari Calcio|Cagliari]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.calciomercato.com/en/news/juventus-and-milan-dealt-blow-as-brescia-will-keep-tonali-38111 |title=Juventus and Milan dealt blow as Brescia will keep Tonali |publisher=calciomercato.com |date=26 August 2019 |access-date=25 September 2019 |archive-date=25 September 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190925044709/https://www.calciomercato.com/en/news/juventus-and-milan-dealt-blow-as-brescia-will-keep-tonali-38111 |url-status=dead }}</ref> On 29 September, he assisted [[Mario Balotelli]]'s goal from a corner kick in a 2–1 away loss to [[SSC Napoli|Napoli]]; he also scored a goal during the match with a powerful shot from outside the area, which was disallowed by [[Video assistant referee|VAR]], however, for a foul by Brescia's [[Dimitri Bisoli]] on Napoli's [[Nikola Maksimović]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.football-italia.net/SerieA/match/142421|title=Napoli 2 – 1 Brescia|publisher=Football Italia|date=29 September 2019|access-date=30 September 2019|archive-date=28 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201028175411/https://www.football-italia.net/SerieA/match/142421|url-status=live}}</ref> He scored his first Serie A goal on 26 October, netting a long-range [[Free kick (association football)|free kick]] into the top corner from the left flank, which was the opening goal in an eventual 3–1 away defeat to [[Genoa CFC|Genoa]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.tsn.ca/juventus-held-to-draw-at-serie-a-struggler-lecce-1.1387599 |title=Juventus held to draw at Serie A struggler Lecce |publisher=TSN |date=26 October 2019 |access-date=26 October 2019 |archive-date=16 September 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200916232435/https://www.tsn.ca/juventus-held-to-draw-at-serie-a-struggler-lecce-1.1387599 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.thescore.com/ita_fed/news/1863673 |title=3 subs, 3 goals as Motta's Genoa debut goes to plan |publisher=The Score |date=26 October 2019 |access-date=26 October 2019 }}</ref>

===AC Milan===
====2020–2021: loan====
On 9 September 2020, Tonali joined [[AC Milan]],<ref>{{Cite web|date=9 September 2020|title=Official Statement: Sandro Tonali|url=https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/media/2020-09-09/official-statement-sandro-tonali|access-date=9 September 2020|website=[[AC Milan]]|archive-date=31 December 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211231204421/https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/media/2020-09-09/official-statement-sandro-tonali|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Tonali ceduto a titolo temporaneo|url=https://www.bresciacalcio.it/news/ultime-news/12888/tonali-ceduto-a-titolo-temporaneo|access-date=2020-09-10|website=bresciacalcio.it|language=it|archive-date=28 October 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211028175418/https://www.bresciacalcio.it/news/ultime-news/12888/tonali-ceduto-a-titolo-temporaneo|url-status=dead}}</ref> on a season-long loan for €10&nbsp;million with an option to buy for €15&nbsp;million, plus bonuses worth €10&nbsp;million.<ref name=":2">{{Cite web|title=Mercato, Tonali al Milan: ci sono firma e annuncio|url=https://www.gazzetta.it/Calcio/Serie-A/Milan/09-09-2020/mercato-tonali-milan-oggi-firma-sandro-si-annuncia-instagram-3801811264648.shtml|access-date=2020-09-10|website=La Gazzetta dello Sport|date=9 September 2020|language=it-IT|archive-date=28 February 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210228024338/https://www.gazzetta.it/Calcio/Serie-A/Milan/09-09-2020/mercato-tonali-milan-oggi-firma-sandro-si-annuncia-instagram-3801811264648.shtml|url-status=live}}</ref> The player will earn a yearly wage of €2&nbsp;million for five years.<ref name=":2" /> Three days later, he made his non-competitive debut in a friendly at [[Milanello]] against his previous club.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.milannews.it/i-tabellini/milan-brescia-3-1-il-tabellino-dell-amichevole-383779|title=Milan-Brescia 3–1: il tabellino dell'amichevole|website=Milan News|access-date=14 September 2020|archive-date=23 April 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210423140726/https://www.milannews.it/i-tabellini/milan-brescia-3-1-il-tabellino-dell-amichevole-383779|url-status=live}}</ref>

Tonali made his competitive debut for Milan on 17 September 2020, coming on as a substitute in the 83rd minute in a 2–0 victory against [[Shamrock Rovers F.C.|Shamrock Rovers FC]] in the second round of Europa League qualifying. He made his Serie A debut for Milan on 21 September 2020, coming off the bench in the 77th minute in a 2–0 victory over [[Bologna FC 1909]] at the [[San Siro]]. Tonali finished the season with 37 appearances, 23 of those in the starting eleven.

==== 2021–2022: Serie A champion ====
[[File:SandroTonali2022Salzburg.jpg|thumb|upright|Tonali lining up for [[AC Milan]] in 2022]]

On 8 July 2021, Milan officially purchased Tonali's rights from Brescia and he signed a five-year contract with the club.<ref>{{cite web|publisher=[[AC Milan]]|url=https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/media/2021-07-08/official-statement-sandro-tonali|title=OFFICIAL STATEMENT: SANDRO TONALI|date=8 July 2021|access-date=8 July 2021|archive-date=8 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210708145938/https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/media/2021-07-08/official-statement-sandro-tonali|url-status=live}}</ref> He took a pay-cut to secure his childhood dream move to Milan and was praised by the fans on social media for this gesture.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://sempremilan.com/tonali-reveals-why-he-accepted-pay-cut-to-stay-at-milan-and-admits-there-were-other-clubs|title=Tonali reveals why he accepted pay cut to stay at Milan and admits:there were other clubs|date=21 July 2021|access-date=25 December 2021|archive-date=25 December 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211225173729/https://sempremilan.com/tonali-reveals-why-he-accepted-pay-cut-to-stay-at-milan-and-admits-there-were-other-clubs|url-status=live}}</ref>

Tonali scored his first goal with Milan's shirt on 29 August 2021 against Cagliari, a free kick that opened the scoresheet in eventual 4–1 win.<ref>{{cite web |title=AC MILAN HIT FOUR IN HOME OPENER |url=https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/serie-a/2021-08-29/ac-milan-hit-four-in-home-opener |website=acmilan |access-date=16 February 2022 |archive-date=17 February 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220217010540/https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/serie-a/2021-08-29/ac-milan-hit-four-in-home-opener |url-status=live }}</ref> On 3 October at [[Stadio Atleti Azzurri d'Italia|Gewiss Stadium]] against Atalanta, Tonali dispossessed the ball from [[Remo Freuler]] and ran to the opponents box to score the second goal in eventual 3–2 victory for Milan.<ref>{{cite web |title=DOMINANT AC MILAN EMERGE VICTORIOUS IN BERGAMO |url=https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/serie-a/2021-10-03/dominant-ac-milan-emerge-victorious-in-bergamo |website=acmilan |access-date=16 February 2022 |archive-date=16 February 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220216135554/https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/serie-a/2021-10-03/dominant-ac-milan-emerge-victorious-in-bergamo |url-status=live }}</ref> On 25 February 2022, Tonali [[Assist (association football)|assisted]] [[Rafael Leão]]'s goal against Udinese, becoming the youngest midfielder to have scored more than one goal (two) and delivered more than one assist (two) in Serie A that season.<ref>{{cite web |title=AC MILAN V UDINESE: THE NUMBERS FROM THE GAME |url=https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/stats/2022-02-25/ac-milan-v-udinese-the-numbers-from-the-game |website=acmilan |access-date=27 February 2022 |archive-date=27 February 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220227083236/https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/stats/2022-02-25/ac-milan-v-udinese-the-numbers-from-the-game |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 24 April as the match against [[SS Lazio|Lazio]] was heading to 1–1 draw, Tonali scored the winner in the stoppage time, securing the lead for his team in Serie A table.<ref>{{cite web |title=COMEBACK IN THE CAPITAL |url=https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/serie-a/2022-04-24/comeback-in-the-capital |website=acmilan |access-date=24 April 2022 |archive-date=24 April 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220424220126/https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/serie-a/2022-04-24/comeback-in-the-capital |url-status=live }}</ref> On 8 May 2022, his 22nd birthday, Tonali scored an equalising and a winning goal in the 3–1 away Serie A victory against [[Hellas Verona FC|Hellas Verona]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Le pagelle di Tonali: siamo a livelli extraterrestre, leader del Diavolo a 22 anni |url=https://www.milannews.it/news/le-pagelle-di-tonali-siamo-a-livelli-extraterrestre-leader-del-diavolo-a-22-anni-451169 |website=MilanNews |access-date=10 May 2022 |archive-date=9 May 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220509140324/https://www.milannews.it/news/le-pagelle-di-tonali-siamo-a-livelli-extraterrestre-leader-del-diavolo-a-22-anni-451169 |url-status=live }}</ref> The comeback victory brought Milan back on top of the Serie A following Inter's 48-hour stay there in a close championship race. Tonali is also the youngest midfielder to have scored five or more goals in Serie A that season (and the second-youngest among all players, older only than Bologna's [[Aaron Hickey]]).<ref>{{cite web |title=HELLAS VERONA V AC MILAN: THE NUMBERS FROM THE GAME |url=https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/stats/2022-05-08/hellas-verona-v-ac-milan-the-numbers-from-the-game |website=ACMILAN |access-date=10 May 2022 |archive-date=8 May 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220508221808/https://www.acmilan.com/en/news/articles/stats/2022-05-08/hellas-verona-v-ac-milan-the-numbers-from-the-game |url-status=live }}</ref> After 3–0 away win against [[US Sassuolo Calcio|Sassuolo]] on 22 May, Milan secured their first Scudetto in 11 years, In total, Tonali played 36 games in the campaign, scoring 5 goals and providing 3 assists.

Tonali's performance that season brought the attention and praise of renowned Italian football pundits, the likes of [[Paolo Di Canio]], [[Roberto Donadoni]] and [[Fabio Capello]], the latter went on to state that Tonali would have found a place in even the greatest of Milan's generation in the past.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Mork |first1=Martin |title=DONADONI AND DI CANIO ON TONALI: 'HE HAS IMPROVED A LOT' |url=https://football-italia.net/donadoni-and-di-canio-on-tonali-he-has-improved-a-lot/ |website=Football Italia |date=4 October 2021 |access-date=16 March 2022 |archive-date=16 March 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220316192125/https://football-italia.net/donadoni-and-di-canio-on-tonali-he-has-improved-a-lot/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Capello: "Rossoneri, la ricetta per vincere. Tonali? avrebbe giocato anche nel grande Milan" |url=https://www.gazzetta.it/Calcio/Serie-A/Milan/16-03-2022/milan-intervista-capello-theo-leao-tonali-kalulu-4301868892474_preview.shtml?reason=unauthenticated&origin=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.gazzetta.it%2FCalcio%2FSerie-A%2FMilan%2F16-03-2022%2Fmilan-intervista-capello-theo-leao-tonali-kalulu-4301868892474.shtml |website=La Gazetta dello Sport |date=16 March 2022 |access-date=16 March 2022 |archive-date=16 March 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220316071816/https://www.gazzetta.it/Calcio/Serie-A/Milan/16-03-2022/milan-intervista-capello-theo-leao-tonali-kalulu-4301868892474_preview.shtml?reason=unauthenticated&origin=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.gazzetta.it%2FCalcio%2FSerie-A%2FMilan%2F16-03-2022%2Fmilan-intervista-capello-theo-leao-tonali-kalulu-4301868892474.shtml |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Newcastle United===
On 3 July 2023, [[Premier League]] club [[Newcastle United F.C.|Newcastle United]] announced the signing of Tonali on a five-year contract, for an undisclosed fee.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.nufc.co.uk/news/latest-news/newcastle-united-sign-sandro-tonali/|title=NEWCASTLE UNITED SIGN SANDRO TONALI|publisher=Newcastle United F.C.|date=3 July 2023|access-date=3 July 2023|archive-date=3 July 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230703164821/https://www.nufc.co.uk/news/latest-news/newcastle-united-sign-sandro-tonali/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=3 July 2023 |title=Newcastle sign Milan midfielder Tonali |language=en-GB |work=BBC Sport |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/66006906 |access-date=2023-07-03 |archive-date=3 July 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230703112124/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/66006906 |url-status=live }}</ref> Reported to be around €70&nbsp;million, this made Tonali the most expensive Italian player of all time.<ref name="transferFee">{{cite web| url = https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/newcastle-sign-tonali-ac-milan-2023-07-03/| title = Newcastle sign Tonali from AC Milan| date = 3 July 2023| website = Reuters.com| access-date = 3 July 2023| archive-date = 3 July 2023| archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20230703164819/https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/newcastle-sign-tonali-ac-milan-2023-07-03/| url-status = live}}</ref>

On 18 July, he made his debut for Newcastle in [[Allan McGregor]]'s testimonial match against [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 July 2023 |title=Rangers 1 Newcastle United 2 |url=https://www.nufc.co.uk/matches/first-team/2023-24/rangers-vs-newcastle-united/ |access-date=2023-07-18 |website=Newcastle United Football Club |language=en |archive-date=18 July 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230718211812/https://www.nufc.co.uk/matches/first-team/2023-24/rangers-vs-newcastle-united/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On 12 August, he scored the opening goal on his Premier League debut in a 5–1 win over [[Aston Villa F.C.|Aston Villa]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2023/aug/12/newcastle-aston-villa-premier-league-match-report |title=Sandro Tonali and Alexander Isak star in Newcastle's rout of Aston Villa |work=The Guardian |date=12 August 2023 |access-date=12 August 2023 |archive-date=13 August 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230813194836/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2023/aug/12/newcastle-aston-villa-premier-league-match-report |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 18 October 2023, Newcastle announced Tonali was being investigated by the Italian Prosecutor's Office and the [[Italian Football Federation]] for alleged illegal betting activity.<ref>{{cite web |title=Sandro Tonali: Newcastle confirm midfielder is being investigated over alleged betting activity |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/67149540 |website=[[BBC Sport]] |access-date=19 October 2023 |date=18 October 2023 |archive-date=19 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231019023739/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/67149540 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 26 October, he was banned from playing football for 10 months for breaching Italian betting regulations. This included eight months in gambling rehabilitation. This meant he would miss the rest of the [[2023–24 Newcastle United F.C. season|2023–24 season]] and [[UEFA Euro 2024]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2023/oct/26/sandro-tonali-newcastle-banned-10-month-over-betting|title=Sandro Tonali: Italian FA agrees 10-month ban for Newcastle footballer|first=Louise|last=Taylor|date=26 October 2023|work=The Guardian}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2023/10/26/sandro-tonali-banned-10-months-newcastle-betting-gambling/|title=Newcastle's Sandro Tonali to miss rest of season and Euro 2024 after 10-month ban for betting breaches|first=Luke|last=Edwards|date=26 October 2023|work=The Daily Telegraph|access-date=26 October 2023|archive-date=26 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231026120150/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2023/10/26/sandro-tonali-banned-10-months-newcastle-betting-gambling/|url-status=live}}</ref> In March 2024, he was charged with misconduct in relation to alleged breaches of the [[The Football Association|Football Association]]'s betting rules. The FA alleged that Tonali broke rules by placing bets on matches between 12 August and 12 October 2023.<ref>{{cite news |title=Sandro Tonali: Newcastle midfielder charged by FA for alleged breaches of betting rules |work=BBC Sport |date=28 March 2024 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/68686129 |access-date=28 March 2024 |archive-date=28 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240328142209/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/68686129 |url-status=live }}</ref> He was handed an additional two-month suspended ban by the FA for these breaches in May 2024, though he was allowed to return to football in August on the condition that no further breaches were made during the 2024–25 season.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.skysports.com/football/news/11678/13127550/sandro-tonali-newcastle-midfielder-handed-two-month-suspended-ban-for-50-breaches-of-fa-betting-rules|title=Sandro Tonali: Newcastle midfielder handed two-month suspended ban for 50 breaches of FA betting rules|website=Sky Sports|access-date=15 June 2024|archive-date=15 June 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240615110402/https://www.skysports.com/football/news/11678/13127550/sandro-tonali-newcastle-midfielder-handed-two-month-suspended-ban-for-50-breaches-of-fa-betting-rules|url-status=live}}</ref>

On 28 August 2024, after serving his suspension, Tonali made his first appearance since October the previous year, playing 61 minutes of a 1–1 draw against [[Nottingham Forest F.C.|Nottingham Forest]] in the third round of the [[2024–25 EFL Cup|EFL Cup]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.skysports.com/football/n-forest-vs-newcastle/report/521197 | title=Nottingham Forest 1–1 Newcastle (3–4 on pens): Sean Longstaff nets winning penalty as Sandro Tonali returns | work=Sky Sports | access-date=29 August 2024 | archive-date=29 August 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240829095310/https://www.skysports.com/football/n-forest-vs-newcastle/report/521197 | url-status=live }}</ref> Four days later, he made his Premier League return, appearing as a 68th minute substitute for [[Sean Longstaff]] in a 2–1 win over [[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cg58p88l784o|title=Newcastle 2–1 Tottenham – Tonali return provides massive boost|date=1 September 2024|access-date=17 September 2024|website=BBC Sport|archive-date=17 September 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240917131004/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cg58p88l784o|url-status=live}}</ref>

On 16 March 2025, Tonali became part of the first Newcastle United side to win a major domestic trophy in 70 years when he played the full 90 minutes in the [[2025 EFL Cup final]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/live/c62zl58dg8qt |website=BBC Football |access-date=21 March 2025 |title=Liverpool 1–2 Newcastle: Magpies win Carabao Cup to end 70-year domestic trophy wait |archive-date=5 September 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250905232101/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/live/c62zl58dg8qt |url-status=live }}</ref> Tonali had scored two goals in the quarter-final against [[Brentford F.C.|Brentford]] to help the club reach the final.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/live/cdekddne4edt |website=BBC Football |access-date=21 March 2025 |title=Newcastle United 3–1 Brentford: Newcastle cruise into Carabao Cup semis |archive-date=21 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250321162643/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/live/cdekddne4edt |url-status=live }}</ref>

In October 2025, it was reported that Tonali had signed a contract extension with Newcastle United during his betting ban, extending his deal until 2029 with an option for a further year to 2030.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kelly |first=Ciaran |date=2025-10-22 |title=Sandro Tonali: Newcastle player signed contract extension during betting ban |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cz6n17d641qo |access-date=2025-10-22 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref>

===Tottenham Hotspur===
On 6 July 2026, Tonali signed for [[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur]] for a transfer fee of £100 million.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.tottenhamhotspur.com/news/1076467/welcome-sandro-tonali-makes-the-move-to-n17|title=Welcome, Sandro! Tonali makes the move to N17|website=Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|date=6 July 2026 |access-date=6 July 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.skysports.com/football/news/11095/13559730/sandro-tonali-tottenham-sign-italy-midfielder-in-club-record-lb100m-deal-from-newcastle|title=Sandro Tonali: Tottenham sign Italy midfielder in club-record £100m deal from Newcastle|website=Sky Sports|date=6 July 2026 |access-date=6 July 2026}}</ref> He made his Spurs debut on 22 August in a 3–0 Premier League defeat to Brentford.<ref>{{Cite web |last=McNulty |first=Phil |date=2026-08-22 |title=Brentford 3-0 Spurs: How the players rated |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cp878q13v72o |access-date=2026-08-25 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref>

== International career ==
[[File:Norway Italy - June 2025 A 30 (cropped).jpg|thumb|upright|Tonali with [[Italy national football team|Italy]] in 2025]]

With the [[Italy national under-19 football team|Italy U19 team]], Tonali took part in the [[2018 UEFA European Under-19 Championship|2018 European Under-19 Championship]], reaching the final of the tournament, where Italy lost 4–3 after [[Overtime (sports)#Association football|extra time]] against [[Portugal national under-19 football team|Portugal]].<ref name="Under-19"/> On 21 March 2019, he made his debut with the [[Italy national under-21 football team|Italy U21]] in a goalless [[Exhibition game#Association football|friendly]] draw against [[Austria national under-21 football team|Austria]] in [[Trieste]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.figc.it/it/nazionali/news/nazionale-u21-a-trieste-e-pari-contro-l-austria-buona-la-prima-mezz-ora-dell-italia-ma-il-match-finisce-a-reti-bianche/ |title=A Trieste è pari contro l'Austria: buona la prima mezz'ora dell'Italia ma il match finisce a reti bianche |publisher=Italian Football Federation |language=it |date=21 March 2019 |access-date=16 October 2019 |archive-date=20 September 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200920201150/https://www.figc.it/it/nazionali/news/nazionale-u21-a-trieste-e-pari-contro-l-austria-buona-la-prima-mezz-ora-dell-italia-ma-il-match-finisce-a-reti-bianche/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Tonali took part in the [[2019 UEFA European Under-21 Championship|2019 European Under-21 Championship]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.figc.it/it/nazionali/news/nazionale-under-21-parte-avventura-europea-di-biagio-ufficializza-la-lista-dei-23-azzurrini/|title=Parte l'avventura europea: Di Biagio ufficializza la lista dei 23 Azzurrini|publisher=Italian Football Federation|language=It|date=6 June 2019|access-date=13 April 2020|archive-date=23 April 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200423162235/https://www.figc.it/it/nazionali/news/nazionale-under-21-parte-avventura-europea-di-biagio-ufficializza-la-lista-dei-23-azzurrini|url-status=live}}</ref>

In November 2018, Tonali received his first call-up to the [[Italy national football team|Italian senior squad]] by manager [[Roberto Mancini]].<ref>{{cite web|date=9 November 2018|title=Nazionale di calcio: Mancini convoca Tonali, Balotelli resta fuori|url=http://www.bsnews.it/2018/11/09/nazionale-calcio-manini-convoca-tonali-balotelli-fuori/|website=BS News|language=it|access-date=10 November 2018|archive-date=14 April 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190414000459/http://www.bsnews.it/2018/11/09/nazionale-calcio-manini-convoca-tonali-balotelli-fuori/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 10 October 2019, after appearing for the Italy U21 team in a goalless draw against [[Republic of Ireland national under-21 football team|Ireland]] in a [[2021 UEFA European Under-21 Championship qualification|European qualifier]], he was called up to the Italy senior squad once again the following day for the team's [[UEFA Euro 2020 qualifying|Euro 2020 qualifiers]] against [[Greece national football team|Greece]] and [[Liechtenstein national football team|Liechtenstein]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.football-italia.net/145138/italy-promote-tonali-seniors|url-status=dead|title=Italy promote Tonali to seniors|website=Football Italia|date=11 October 2019|access-date=12 October 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191022010648/https://football-italia.net/145138/italy-promote-tonali-seniors|archive-date=22 October 2019}}</ref>

Tonali made his senior international debut on 15 October 2019, coming on as a substitute in the 5–0 away victory against Liechtenstein in [[Vaduz]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.football-italia.net/145285/historic-manita-liechtenstein|url-status=dead|title=Historic manita in Liechtenstein|website=Football Italia|date=15 October 2019|access-date=16 October 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200102060149/https://football-italia.net/145285/historic-manita-liechtenstein|archive-date=2 January 2020}}</ref> On 15 November, he started for the team in a 3–0 away victory against [[Bosnia and Herzegovina national football team|Bosnia and Herzegovina]] of the same tournament.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.football-italia.net/146483/italy-dominant-display-bosnia|url-status=dead|title=Italy: Dominant display in Bosnia|website=Football Italia |date=15 November 2019 |access-date=15 November 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200802024453/https://football-italia.net/146483/italy-dominant-display-bosnia|archive-date=2 August 2020}}</ref>

==Style of play==
Regarded as a promising player in his youth by the media, Tonali has been described by pundits as a ''[[Playmaker#Deep-lying playmakers|regista]]'',<ref>{{cite web|date=20 September 2018|title=Agent: 'Tonali better than Pirlo!'|url=https://www.football-italia.net/128253/agent-%E2%80%98tonali-better-pirlo%E2%80%99|access-date=14 October 2018|publisher=Football Italia|archive-date=16 September 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200916163217/https://www.football-italia.net/128253/agent-%E2%80%98tonali-better-pirlo%E2%80%99|url-status=live}}</ref> although he is also described as a versatile midfielder, who is capable of playing in several roles.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/4989200/2023/10/24/newcastle-sandro-tonali-replacement-transfer/ |title=How Newcastle could replace Sandro Tonali: Signings, loans and Saudi Arabia |work=The Athletic |last1=Whitehead |first1=Jacob |date=24 October 2023 |access-date=29 November 2023 |archive-date=20 January 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250120104318/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/4989200/2023/10/24/newcastle-sandro-tonali-replacement-transfer/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In his youth, he was often likened to [[Andrea Pirlo]] – who also started his career with [[Brescia Calcio|Brescia]] – in terms of his movement, coordination, appearance, technical qualities, position, and playing style.<ref name="next Pirlo" /><ref name="Brescia back in business" /><ref name=":0">{{cite web|author1=Angelo Taglieri|date=30 July 2018|title=Inter, Juve e Roma avvisate: per Tonali Cellino studia un affare alla Nainggolan|url=https://www.calciomercato.com/news/inter-juve-e-roma-avvisate-per-tonali-cellino-studia-un-affare-a-90797|access-date=14 October 2018|publisher=calciomercato.com|language=Italian|archive-date=16 September 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200916200748/https://www.calciomercato.com/news/inter-juve-e-roma-avvisate-per-tonali-cellino-studia-un-affare-a-90797|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|author1=Gian Paolo Laffranchi|date=5 February 2018|title=Brescia al passo di Tonali in viaggio sulle orme di Pirlo|url=http://www.bresciaoggi.it/home/sport/brescia-calcio/brescia-al-passo-di-tonali-in-viaggio-sulle-orme-di-pirlo-1.6277956|access-date=14 October 2018|publisher=bresciaoggi.it|language=Italian|archive-date=1 April 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190401193510/http://www.bresciaoggi.it/home/sport/brescia-calcio/brescia-al-passo-di-tonali-in-viaggio-sulle-orme-di-pirlo-1.6277956|url-status=dead}}</ref> Considered to be a strong, fast, energetic, elegant, and creative midfielder, with an ability to read the game,<ref name=":1" /> Tonali usually plays in a [[Midfielder#Central midfielder|central]] or [[Midfielder#Defensive midfielder|defensive midfield]] role as a [[Midfielder#Deep-lying playmaker (Strolling 10)|deep-lying playmaker]] in a [[Formation (association football)#4–3–3|4–3–3 formation]].<ref>{{cite web|author1=Fabio Pettenò|date=9 July 2018|title=Brescia, rifondazione in atto: cambia più di metà squadra|url=http://www.bresciaoggi.it/home/sport/brescia-calcio/brescia-rifondazione-in-atto-cambia-pi%C3%B9-di-met%C3%A0-squadra-1.6621603|access-date=14 October 2018|publisher=bresciaoggi.it|language=Italian|archive-date=1 April 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190401193508/http://www.bresciaoggi.it/home/sport/brescia-calcio/brescia-rifondazione-in-atto-cambia-pi%C3%B9-di-met%C3%A0-squadra-1.6621603|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Alessandro Rubichini|date=7 September 2018|title=Analisi del Singolo: Sandro Tonali del Brescia|url=https://assoanalisti.it/analisi-del-singolo-sandro-tonali-del-brescia/|access-date=2020-08-12|website=AIAPC|language=it-IT|archive-date=30 September 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200930061621/https://assoanalisti.it/analisi-del-singolo-sandro-tonali-del-brescia/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Bresciaingol – Brescia calcio – News, esclusive, diretta partita, calcio mercato, giovanili, calcio femminile|url=http://www.bresciaingol.com/news.asp?id_news=29603|access-date=2020-08-12|website=bresciaingol.com|archive-date=16 September 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200916211908/http://www.bresciaingol.com/news.asp?id_news=29603|url-status=dead}}</ref> Dictating plays for Brescia with his passing in midfield, he set up two goals and scored two himself in his 19 appearances in Serie B during the 2017–18 season.<ref name="next Pirlo" /><ref name="tuttocalciatori">{{cite web|title=Sandro Tonali|url=https://www.tuttocalciatori.net/Tonali_Sandro|access-date=14 October 2018|publisher=tuttocalciatori.net|language=Italian|archive-date=27 October 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211027203909/https://www.tuttocalciatori.net/Tonali_Sandro|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=":0" /> Although naturally right-footed, he is known for his long passing ability with either foot.<ref name=":1">{{cite web |url=https://www.calcionews24.com/sandro-tonali-caratteristiche-tecniche-ruolo |title=Chi è Sandro Tonali, il piccoletto che studia da Pirlo |publisher=calcionews24.com |language=Italian |last1=Piazzola |first1=Andrea |date=30 October 2018 |access-date=30 September 2019 |archive-date=12 September 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210912104432/https://www.calcionews24.com/sandro-tonali-caratteristiche-tecniche-ruolo/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Moreover, he is also adept at taking [[Set piece (football)|set-pieces]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.90min.com/posts/why-sandro-tonali-could-become-a-better-player-than-andrea-pirlo-01e86nxz51wt |title=Why Sandro Tonali Could Become a Better Player Than Andrea Pirlo |publisher=90min.com |last1=Bushe |first1=Lee |date=13 May 2020 |access-date=14 November 2021 |archive-date=14 November 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211114064939/https://www.90min.com/posts/why-sandro-tonali-could-become-a-better-player-than-andrea-pirlo-01e86nxz51wt |url-status=live }}</ref> He is also known to play as a [[Midfielder#Box-to-box midfielder|box-to-box midfielder]], while his creativity, ability to find space, make late runs, and his penchant for driving forward with the ball saw him deployed in a more [[Midfielder#Attacking midfielder|advanced]] role on occasion at Milan under manager [[Stefano Pioli]], namely as a ''[[Midfielder#Mezzala|mezzala]]''.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/37586725/tonali-arrival-gives-milan-glimpse-their-bright-new-dawn-horizon |title=Tonali's arrival gives Milan a glimpse of their bright new dawn on the horizon |publisher=ESPN |date=9 September 2020 |access-date=29 November 2023 |archive-date=3 June 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250603182959/https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/37586725/tonali-arrival-gives-milan-glimpse-their-bright-new-dawn-horizon |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://football-italia.net/how-tonali-can-guide-newcastle-to-victory-in-milan/ |title=UCL: How Tonali can guide Newcastle to victory in Milan |publisher=Football Italia |last1=Heyes |first1=Apollo |date=September 2023 |access-date=29 November 2023 |archive-date=6 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240106170817/https://football-italia.net/how-tonali-can-guide-newcastle-to-victory-in-milan/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

In addition to Pirlo, Tonali has also cited [[Steven Gerrard]] and [[Luka Modrić]] as influences, and has also compared his own playing style to that of [[Gennaro Gattuso]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.calciomercato.com/en/news/brescia-tonali-i-am-ready-for-the-serie-a-pirlo-i-am-more-like-g-50569 |title=Brescia, Tonali: 'I am ready for the Serie A. Pirlo? I am more like Gattuso...' |publisher=calciomercato.com |date=27 July 2019 |access-date=30 September 2019 |archive-date=25 September 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190925044733/https://www.calciomercato.com/en/news/brescia-tonali-i-am-ready-for-the-serie-a-pirlo-i-am-more-like-g-50569 |url-status=dead }}</ref> In July 2019, he was named by [[UEFA]] as one of the 50 promising young players to watch for the 2019–20 season.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0253-0e99d077bac2-c2ee61198ae0-1000--50-for-the-future-uefa-com-s-ones-to-watch-in-2019-20/ |title=50 for the future: UEFA.com's ones to watch in 2019/20 |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=30 July 2019 |access-date=30 September 2019 |archive-date=1 June 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200601090300/https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0253-0e99d077bac2-c2ee61198ae0-1000--50-for-the-future-uefa-com-s-ones-to-watch-in-2019-20/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

==Personal life==
Tonali has been an [[AC Milan]] fan since childhood.<ref>{{cite web |title=GdS: Milan fans are crazy about Tonali and his incredible growth this season |url=https://sempremilan.com/gds-milan-fans-are-crazy-about-tonali-and-his-incredible-growth-this-season |website=sempremilan |date=6 November 2021 |access-date=16 February 2022 |archive-date=16 February 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220216233331/https://sempremilan.com/gds-milan-fans-are-crazy-about-tonali-and-his-incredible-growth-this-season |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Yokhin |first1=Michael |title=AC Milan: Is Sandro Tonali the new Andrea Pirlo? |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/58549032 |access-date=16 February 2022 |publisher=BBC |date=15 September 2021 |archive-date=16 February 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220216233912/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/58549032 |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 1 July 2025, Tonali married Juliette Pastore.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.chroniclelive.co.uk/news/showbiz-news/sandro-tonali-wedding-juliette-pastore-31977676.amp|title=Newcastle's Sandro Tonali marries Giulia Pastore in firework drenched Italian ceremony|date=2 July 2025|publisher=chroniclelive|access-date=10 January 2026|archive-date=5 July 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250705190802/https://www.chroniclelive.co.uk/news/showbiz-news/sandro-tonali-wedding-juliette-pastore-31977676.amp|url-status=live}}</ref> On 8 January 2026, they welcomed their first child, Leonardo.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://football-italia.net/tonali-announces-personal-news-half-time-sub/|title=Tonali announces personal news after half-time withdrawal in Newcastle 4-3 Leeds|publisher=Football Italia|date=9 January 2026|access-date=10 January 2026|archive-date=12 January 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260112033311/https://football-italia.net/tonali-announces-personal-news-half-time-sub/amp/|url-status=live}}</ref>

